ov/ozone- pollution-and-your-health\n\nHEALTH INFORMATION...Increasing likelihood of respiratory symptoms\nand breathing discomfort in active children and adults and people\nwith lung disease, such as asthma. Active children and adults, and\npeople with lung disease, such as asthma, should reduce prolonged\nor heavy outdoor exertion.","ends":"2026-08-28T16:00:00-06:00","severity":"Unknown","areaDesc":"Broomfield, CO; Jefferson, CO; Denver, CO; Douglas, CO; Adams, CO; Boulder, CO; Weld, CO; Larimer, CO; Arapahoe, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a17a27b506afd523954d57cd2deb7b4d9d4ce26d.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a17a27b506afd523954d57cd2deb7b4d9d4ce26d.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-28T11:43:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KBOU 281143 AFDBOU Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Denver/Boulder CO 543 AM MDT Fri Aug 28 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Isolated/scattered high based showers/storms Friday with gusty winds. - Temperatures return to the 90s Friday and Saturday across the plains. - Thunderstorm coverage increases for late Saturday through Monday. && .DISCUSSION /Through Thursday/... Issued at","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-28T08:41:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Today and tonight...Warm and dry conditions are forecast today, with temperatures likely reaching the low to mid 90s across the lower elevations. Daytime minimum relative humidity will reach about 15-25% across most of the lower elevations and high mountain valleys. Scattered high based showers and a few thunderstorms are possible this afternoon, with variable and gusty outflow winds","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":{"station_id":"cht01","station_name":"Chatfield at South Platte Reservoir","distance_km":15.4,"soil_temp_5cm_f":74.97,"soil_temp_15cm_f":